  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 306 AM EDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nThe long-term outlook consists of a strengthening ridge that will \nbuild through the weekend. Models depict an incremental decrease in \nprecipitation by the time we reach the weekend; however, they tend \nto undersell the effects of a persistent NW flow and associated MCS \ndevelopments that are common in these environments. That being \nthe case, there is at least a chance of seeing a more active \ndiurnal convective pattern even as temperatures climb in response \nto the building ridge. One possible silver lining is that, if \nconvection is more active than expected, we will likely see \nslightly lower afternoon temperatures through the weekend. \n\nRegardless, the risk of excessive heat will ramp up each day, \nwith some areas reaching the mid-to-upper 90s by Friday. Most of \nthe CWA can expect apparent temperatures in the triple digits, \nwith the central and eastern portions of the forecast area \nreaching Heat Advisory criteria. We will need to keep an eye on \ntemperatures over the period, and the heat should be a \nconsideration when making plans for outdoor activities.",
